<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francis Dhanis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1862">1862</a>–<a href="/years/1909">1909</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francis Dhanis was a Belgian officer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-free-state">Congo Free State</a> who commanded its forces in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-arab-war">Congo Arab war</a> of 1892–1894, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nyangwe">Nyangwe</a> and Kasongo. In 1896 he led a large expedition towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>, which collapsed in 1897 when its Tetela soldiers mutinied. He was made a baron and later served as vice-governor-general.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francis-dhanis.jpg" alt="Francis Dhanis" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown, before 1909; published in 1913 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BaronDhanisGala.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
